nce the zoomed image exceeds the container size, and this only happens when using wgpu as the rendering backend.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2611f619-bb9a-44d7-b167-987f703470ec\n\na minimal repo for the issue: [https://github.com/stevekki/iced_viewer_issue](https://github.com/stevekki/iced_viewer_issue)\n\nRun the example with this command: ```ICED_BACKEND=wgpu cargo run```\n\nmain.rs\n\n```rust\nuse iced::{\n    Length,\n    widget::image::{Handle, Viewer},\n};\n\npub fn main() -> iced::Result {\n    iced::application(App::new, App::update, App::view).run()\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\nenum Message {}\n\nstruct App {\n    handle: Handle,\n}\n\nimpl App {\n    fn new() -> Self {\n        Self {\n            handle: Handle::from_path(\"images/ferris.png\"),\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn update(&mut self, _: Message) {}\n\n    fn view(&self) -> iced::Element<'_, Message> {\n        Viewer::new(self.handle.clone())\n            .width(Length::Fill)\n            .height(Length::Fill)\n            .into()\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### What is the expected behavior?\n\nWhen the zoomed image exceeds the container, it should not be cropped at the bottom or right edges.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/86bf4bc7-a651-419a-ada5-f74628884425\n\n### Version\n\nmaster\n\n### Operating System\n\nLinux\n\n### Do you have any log output?\n\n```shell\n\n```","closed_by":{"login":"hecrj","id":518289,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxODI4OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/518289?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hecrj","html_url":"https://github.com/hecrj","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hecrj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hecrj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hecrj/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hecrj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hecrj/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https